<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">September 18, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 203 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-09-18T09:00:00+02:00</span> &middot; Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v49.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">&#9878; Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge &middot; forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL (written LAST by Judge) ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      UNGA high-level week (Sep 18–28) places Pezeshkian and Araghchi in New York for the first time since the war began; <span class="cite">F4</span> collapsed from 22% to 8% as active naval combat extended through Sep 16 with no Hormuz recovery pathway, while <span class="cite">F5</span> slipped to 33% as Yashar leads Likud in 4 of 5 polls with 39 days to the October 27 election.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>&#9888; DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until &ge;20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline &mdash; any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">5 active &middot; last reasoned 2026-09-18</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM ≤72h -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">Near-term &mdash; resolves &le;72h</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8 &middot; 2026-09-18-iran-us-unga-contact-confirmed-by-sep21</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a named US official and a named Iranian official publicly confirm a direct communication or in-person contact during UNGA high-level week before EOD 2026-09-21?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">28%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-09-21</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 72h forecast. Trump Sep 16 claimed Iran contacted the US &lsquo;directly&rsquo;; US granted visas to Pezeshkian and Araghchi on Sep 17 for UNGA. Both delegations arrive in New York Sep 18, removing the logistical barrier to contact. UNGA margins historically function as ad-hoc contact venues during adversarial periods. Active kinetic exchange and domestic political constraints cap probability; public confirmation requires both parties to acknowledge a politically sensitive event.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if, before EOD 2026-09-21, a named US official (Secretary of State, NSC Director, or Special Envoy) AND a named Iranian official (FM Araghchi or President Pezeshkian) each publicly confirm — or if two independent TIER1 sources simultaneously report — that a direct communication or in-person meeting occurred during UNGA high-level week.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two independent TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/Al Jazeera/NYT/BBC), OR one TIER1 + one official statement (US State Dept, Iranian MFA, or IRNA/Tasnim quoting a named official).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Trump's unilateral claim without Iranian confirmation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Mediator-only readout without US or Iranian named-official confirmation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Protocol encounters in shared UN sessions without deliberate bilateral exchange do not count.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Named US official confirms UNGA-margin contact with Iran</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Named Iranian official (Araghchi/Pezeshkian) confirms UNGA contact</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">US-Iran mutual 48h kinetic pause prior to Sep 21</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 Days</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F9 &middot; 2026-09-18-pezeshkian-unga-ceasefire-proposal-by-sep25</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Pezeshkian deliver an explicit, named ceasefire proposal — referencing the Islamabad MoU or new specific terms — in his UNGA General Debate speech before EOD 2026-09-25?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">44%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-09-25</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 7-day forecast. Iran's consistent posture since Sep 1 SCO: conditional return to Islamabad MoU &lsquo;if US does.&rsquo; UNGA is the highest-visibility multilateral venue Iran has available; Pezeshkian's speech is the first opportunity to address the full UN membership since the war began. Iranian state media has treated the Islamabad MoU as a binding international agreement. P=0.44 reflects that a conditional MoU restoration offer likely meets the resolution threshold, tempered by the possibility of a more combative tone given the Sep 5–16 escalation cycle.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Pezeshkian's UNGA General Debate speech, delivered before EOD 2026-09-25, contains an explicit named ceasefire proposal referencing Islamabad MoU restoration or new specific terms (named conditions, timeline, or mediator), and the speech text is carried by IRNA/Tasnim as an official statement. A general call for 'peace' without named conditions = NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Full speech text from IRNA/Tasnim OR United Nations verbatim records (un.org), corroborated by one TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Speech referencing MoU purely as US accusation without forward-looking offer = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. If Pezeshkian is interrupted or speech not officially transmitted: AMBIGUOUS pending UN transcript.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Pezeshkian confirmed scheduled UNGA speech (~Sep 22-23)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Araghchi pre-speech statement naming MoU restoration</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">US-Iran kinetic exchange continues through Sep 22 with no pause</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F10 &middot; 2026-09-18-iran-oman-hormuz-corridor-plan-published-by-oct2</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Iran-Oman joint Hormuz maritime corridor plan be officially published (maps and joint statement released publicly) before EOD 2026-10-02?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">27%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-10-02</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New 14-day forecast. Araghchi confirmed Sep 13 that Iran and Oman had &lsquo;agreed to establish a new route and prepared the relevant maps and a joint statement.&rsquo; The document exists. Publication is Iran&rsquo;s next diplomatic signaling option. Oman&rsquo;s interest in publication is high (managing Gulf shipping impact). Counter-pressure: Iran may withhold as a UNGA negotiating asset; IRGC may resist any document appearing to offer Hormuz concessions.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if, before EOD 2026-10-02, official text of an Iran-Oman joint statement on Hormuz maritime corridor arrangements, including or accompanied by referenced maps, is published by IRNA, Oman News Agency, or a named Omani/Iranian ministerial statement.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IRNA or Oman News Agency primary publication, corroborated by one TIER1 within 24h.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>A communiqué referencing a 'plan' without publishing specific terms or maps = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Maps published without joint statement, or vice versa = AMBIGUOUS pending second component within 72h. Unilateral Iranian statement without Omani co-signature = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Araghchi or Omani FM confirms imminent publication timeline</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">UNGA-margin Iran-Oman bilateral meeting held (Sep 18-28)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC public statement opposing Hormuz partial reopening plan</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4 &middot; 2026-09-03-hormuz-30-transits-by-oct3</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz reach &ge;30 vessels/day (7-day rolling average) before EOD 2026-10-03?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">8%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">&darr; &minus;14pp from 22% (2026-09-03)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-10-03</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Severe downward revision (0.22&rarr;0.08). Sep 5–8: CENTCOM destroyed 8 Iranian tankers across two retaliatory operations after IRGC ballistic-missile attacks on US warships, including a carrier-targeting attack Sep 16. Hormuz daily transits: 7 (Sep 9), 4 (Sep 15), 12 (Sep 16). 7-day rolling average approximately 6–9 vessels, 5–7% of pre-war normal. Araghchi (Sep 13, Muscat) confirmed the Iran-Oman corridor plan requires US Islamabad MoU compliance before Hormuz reopens. No insurer has reinstated P&amp;I war-risk cover. UNGA window and pre-negotiated corridor plan preserve a small tail preventing collapse to near-zero, but the 30-vessel target has no available pathway in 15 days.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if any AIS-based ship-tracking source (IMF PortWatch, Straits.live, MarineTraffic, Lloyd's List Intelligence) records &ge;30 commercial transits/day as a 7-day rolling average at any point between 2026-09-03 and 2026-10-03. 7-day rolling window must close by EOD Oct 3.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>AIS-based tracker + one TIER1 or OSINT confirmation (Bloomberg/Reuters/Lloyd's List).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Naval escort vessels and warships do not count toward commercial transit; if trackers diverge by &gt;20%, flag AMBIGUOUS. 7-day rolling window must close by EOD Oct 3; partial windows do not resolve YES.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-CONTRADICTED">Sustained 72h halt in Iranian mine/vessel-attack activity</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">P&amp;I war-risk cover reinstated by a named insurer</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM/mediator-confirmed Iranian commitment to halt mine deployment</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Iran-Oman corridor plan prepared (maps + draft statement exist; not published)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 Days</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5 &middot; 2026-09-03-likud-plurality-oct27-election</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Likud win the most Knesset seats (seat plurality) in the October 27, 2026 Israeli election?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">33%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">&darr; &minus;9pp from 42% (2026-09-03)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&rarr; resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Update (0.42&rarr;0.33). Sep 17 polling consolidation: four of five polls show Yashar at 22 seats ahead of Likud at 18 as the modal result; only i24NEWS shows Likud at 27 vs Yashar 22. Channel 13 projects Netanyahu bloc 54 vs Eisenkot bloc 52, but the individual party race favors Yashar in modal polling. The &lsquo;PARTIAL&rsquo; indicator on Likud &ge;23 seats no longer holds on the balance of polling evidence. 39 days remain; Israeli wartime polling carries historical uncertainty; the i24NEWS outlier and bloc arithmetic prevent a sharper move.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if official Israeli Central Elections Committee results show Likud winning more seats than any other single party in the October 27, 2026 election.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Israeli Central Elections Committee official results, carried by Times of Israel/Haaretz/Reuters/AP.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If Likud and one other party tie on seats: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO (plurality requires strict advantage over every other single party). Exit polls alone do not resolve; official preliminary results suffice if published before EOD Oct 27.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-CONTRADICTED">Polls showing Likud &ge;23 seats, ahead of Yashar (4/5 polls CONTRADICTED; i24NEWS outlier excepted)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Likud bloc forms coalition-eligible alliance pre-election</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Eisenkot/Yashar polling surge &gt;25 seats (modal at 22; Maariv showed 24)</span>
        </div>
